# Next.js App Router Root Layout (Concrete Rule)

**Mandate:** When generating or editing `app/layout.tsx` or `src/app/layout.tsx`, GRIP MUST follow the Next.js App Router layout rules exactly. Violations cause `ReferenceError: children is not defined` and "You're using next/head inside the app directory" warnings.

## Rules

1. **Define `children` in the function signature.**  
   The root layout MUST receive `children` as a prop. Write:
   ```ts
   export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
     return (
       <html lang="en">
         <body>{children}</body>
       </html>
     )
   }
   ```
   Do NOT use `{children}` in JSX without defining it in the function parameters.

2. **Do NOT use `next/head` or `<Head>` in the app directory.**  
   The App Router does not allow it. Use the **Metadata API** instead:
   ```ts
   import type { Metadata } from "next"
   export const metadata: Metadata = {
     title: "App Title",
     description: "App description",
   }
   ```
   Never `import Head from 'next/head'` in files under `app/` or `src/app/`.

3. **Return only `<html>` and `<body>`; do not wrap in fragment or `<main>`.**  
   The root layout must return exactly:
   ```tsx
   return (
     <html lang="en">
       <body>{children}</body>
     </html>
   )
   ```
   Do NOT return `<><Head /><main><html>...</html></main></>` or any structure that wraps `<html>` inside `<main>` or a React fragment.

## Correct example

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next"

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "App Title",
  description: "App description",
}

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body className="min-h-screen">{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

## Do NOT

- Use `{children}` without defining `children` in the function parameters.
- Import or use `next/head` or `<Head>` in app/layout.tsx or any file under app/.
- Return a fragment (`<>...</>`) or wrap `<html>` inside `<main>` in the root layout.

## Where this is enforced

- **buildQualityPlan.ts:** `MANDATORY_GRIP_NEXTJS_APP_ROUTER_LAYOUT` injected in planGeneratorService, enhanced-chat, and legal-sandbox chat.
- **templateEngineService:** When generating full-file for `app/layout.tsx` or `src/app/layout.tsx`, the full-file prompt includes a CRITICAL block with these layout rules.
- **MANDATORY_GRIP_PRODUCTION_READINESS** references this rule for Next.js App Router.
- **CONCRETE-RULES-AND-ALIGNMENT.md** and **.cursorrules** document this rule.
